    "hang_s_<edge>": "maximum dead-hang time on a given fingerboard edge (climber finger strength-endurance)",
    "climb_grade_<discipline>": "hardest route / boulder sent, per discipline (lead, boulder)",
    "neck_cm": "neck circumference (hand-logged girth; grappler neck development)",
    "carry_kg_m_<carry>": "loaded carry load x distance (farmer / sandbag / bear-hug carry)",
    "row_m_week": "weekly rowing distance (erg or water)",
    "ftp_w_per_kg": "cycling functional threshold power relative to body weight",
    "ride_km_week": "weekly riding distance",
    "balance_s_single_leg": "single-leg balance hold time (eyes open/closed stated)",
    "agility_s_<test>": "change-of-direction test time (e.g. 5-0-5, spider drill)"
  },
  "rules": [
    "one named ideal = one strand with its own measure; never blend ideals into one number",
    "a strand whose measure is missing is carried as a direction with the gap named, never proxied by body_fat_pct",
    "Pilates maps to slow, controlled, full-range movement (controlled_tempo_share_sets), NOT to timed isometric holds (zero_load_control_share_sets)",
    "X-taper != V-taper: the X includes judged legs; its measure includes skeletal_muscle_kg and segmental leg lean mass, not body fat alone",
    "real conflicts (energy direction, body-weight direction, time) go to the ORDER choice, not a blended target",
    "grappler (047) != combat/striking (044): force-first, grip/isometric, body weight may go UP; MMA stays on 044",
    "zero_load_control_share_sets is a PARTIAL fit where holding is the work (climber hangs, grappler holds, ski low holds) and never the Pilates measure",
    "weight-sensitive sports (044, 047, 049 lightweight, 046, 050, 051): coach the strength/skill side of the ratio; acute cuts and restriction are the caught route (exercise/harm-route-boundary-031)",
    "sport rows 046-053: the sport is the primary practice; the gym strand supports with transferable strength and the row's injury-specific work; ski/snowboard enters as a pre-season block"
  ],
